Beryllium: WebGPU is off unless asked for

Purpose: plan/18 section 7, decided by the owner on 11 November 2026
  (feature matrix F-GPU-02: "finds an adapter, or is turned off deliberately
  and documented"). WebGPU gives every web page a second way into the GPU
  process: Dawn, then Vulkan, then the driver. That process is not confined
  on FreeBSD and will stay so with NVIDIA's driver. As built, the status
  page listed WebGPU as enabled while pages were given no adapter, because
  Chromium gives Linux and the BSDs an adapter only when the GPU process
  composites with Vulkan, which it does not here. Nobody had chosen either
  half of that.
  - gpu/config/gpu_finch_features.cc: on FreeBSD the features WebGPUService
    and WebGPUBlobCache are disabled by default. Elsewhere nothing changes.
  To turn it on: --enable-features=WebGPUService. That exposes the GPU
    process to WebGPU content, and on this configuration it is not known to
    produce an adapter at all (plan/18 section 7.3, step 1, not yet run).
Stage: 4 (Beryllium series). Applies over the BSD patch for this file
  (stage 2).
Refreshed against: Chromium 156.0.8078.79, Helium 0.20.3 (2f81b9ca),
  FreeBSD ports 6ad3e0c8, using freebsd/tools/patch-workbench. Not yet
  compiled (written for build 0.20.3.21).
Test: freebsd/tests/browser/tests/test_40_rendering.py test_gpu_info
  records the feature status the GPU page gives for webgpu, and
  test_webgl_webgpu_canvas what a page gets from navigator.gpu; from this
  build the first must not say enabled. What a page then sees (no
  navigator.gpu, or no adapter) is recorded, not yet asserted.
security-review: not required (turns a feature off by default; no new input
  handling)

--- a/gpu/config/gpu_finch_features.cc
+++ b/gpu/config/gpu_finch_features.cc
@@ -289,7 +289,14 @@
 
 // Enable WebGPU on gpu service side only. This is used with origin trial and
 // enabled by default on supported platforms.
-#if BUILDFLAG(IS_APPLE) || BUILDFLAG(IS_WIN) || BUILDFLAG(IS_CHROMEOS) || \
+#if BUILDFLAG(IS_FREEBSD)
+// Beryllium: off unless asked for (--enable-features=WebGPUService). WebGPU
+// gives every page a second way into the GPU process (Dawn, then Vulkan,
+// then the driver), and that process is not confined on FreeBSD. As built,
+// it was reported as enabled while pages were given no adapter, which
+// nobody chose (plan/18 section 7; feature matrix F-GPU-02).
+#define WEBGPU_ENABLED base::FEATURE_DISABLED_BY_DEFAULT
+#elif BUILDFLAG(IS_APPLE) || BUILDFLAG(IS_WIN) || BUILDFLAG(IS_CHROMEOS) || \
     BUILDFLAG(IS_ANDROID) || BUILDFLAG(USE_WEBGPU_ON_VULKAN_VIA_GL_INTEROP)
 #define WEBGPU_ENABLED base::FEATURE_ENABLED_BY_DEFAULT
 #else
